  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">When a team spends more time debugging retries, lost state, and invisible run status than building the agent's actual logic, that's the real signal it's time to graduate to a hosted platform, not a fixed timeline or team size.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Watch four recurring needs specifically — persistence, retries, observability, and scaling — and graduate once you're hitting real production pain on two or more of them, rather than hypothesizing about the need in advance.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Graduating moves orchestration responsibility to the platform, not the agent's decision logic, which stays yours — and it doesn't make an unsafe-to-retry side effect safe by itself, so idempotency still needs deliberate design at the step level.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
